Creating the fagioli, the fagioli are fantastic.

514
00:36:02,200 --> 00:36:05,560
While these Italian heirloom beans can provide the main entree,

515
00:36:05,561 --> 00:36:08,380
this little red bean can serve as the dessert.

516
00:36:10,080 --> 00:36:13,720
Believed to have originated in Asia over 4,000 years ago,

517
00:36:14,380 --> 00:36:18,480
the izuki bean is Japan's second most popular legume after the soybean.

518
00:36:19,660 --> 00:36:20,860
Sweeter than most other beans,

519
00:36:21,620 --> 00:36:24,740
the izuki is most often found in traditional Japanese pastries,

520
00:36:25,300 --> 00:36:26,720
known as wagashi.

521
00:36:28,900 --> 00:36:32,040
Located in the heart of Los Angeles' little Tokyo district,

522
00:36:33,040 --> 00:36:36,700
Mikawaya has been baking and selling wagashi since 1910.

523
00:36:38,480 --> 00:36:42,080
The filling in more than half of Mikawaya's 40 different pastries

524
00:36:42,081 --> 00:36:44,800
is a paste made from azuki beans.

525
00:36:45,400 --> 00:36:50,020
The basic filling for Japanese pastries is anko,

526
00:36:50,280 --> 00:36:52,460
which is made from azuki bean.

527
00:36:52,740 --> 00:36:55,980
We have different pastries that uses the whole bean,

528
00:36:56,360 --> 00:36:57,980
which is called tsubushi an.

529
00:36:57,981 --> 00:37:06,860
And then we have pastries that use just a string form of azuki, and that's called koshi-an.

530
00:37:09,220 --> 00:37:13,720
Mikowaya starts each batch of bean paste with 150 pounds of azuki beans.

531
00:37:16,920 --> 00:37:24,860
We soak the azuki in water, and then we cook it for about three hours, and then we add sugar to it.

532
00:37:24,861 --> 00:37:28,000
And this is the finished product.

533
00:37:29,500 --> 00:37:32,440
Many of the pastries also include sweetened mochi,

534
00:37:33,000 --> 00:37:35,140
a sticky cake made from rice.

535
00:37:36,340 --> 00:37:39,440
In this case, we're making my machine.

536
00:37:39,800 --> 00:37:44,080
The outside is sweet rice, and then we have the azuki,

537
00:37:44,360 --> 00:37:45,860
which is the filling.

538
00:37:46,240 --> 00:37:48,660
And this machine actually encrusted,

539
00:37:49,000 --> 00:37:52,480
and it comes out where the mochi is on the outside

540
00:37:52,481 --> 00:37:54,100
and the bean paste is on the inside.

541
00:37:54,101 --> 00:37:55,940
It's called gyuhi.

542
00:37:55,941 --> 00:38:00,560
We can produce 2,000 in one hour with this machine.

543
00:38:01,600 --> 00:38:06,200
This particular pastry is called ohagi or botamochi.

544
00:38:06,201 --> 00:38:10,780
And the unusual part is the bean paste is on the outside

545
00:38:10,781 --> 00:38:13,340
and rice is in the inside.

546
00:38:13,341 --> 00:38:17,380
So a lot of kids say it's inside out mochi.

547
00:38:17,381 --> 00:38:20,100
It has a distinct flavor, a subtle flavor.

548
00:38:20,101 --> 00:38:24,020
Once you eat it, you'll know the flavor of azuki.

549
00:38:24,021 --> 00:38:26,560
but it's always been in Japanese pastries.

550
00:38:26,561 --> 00:38:29,920
Mikowaya doesn't confine the azuki bean to its pastries.

551
00:38:29,921 --> 00:38:32,560
We are the creators of mochi ice cream,

552
00:38:32,561 --> 00:38:36,160
which is a traditional Japanese pastry on the outside,

553
00:38:36,161 --> 00:38:39,840
the mochi, and the inside is ice cream.

554
00:38:39,841 --> 00:38:44,780
In the case of azuki, we actually created azuki ice cream.

555
00:38:46,000 --> 00:38:48,440
Mikowaya completed one century

556
00:38:48,441 --> 00:38:50,480
and plans to be around for another,

557
00:38:50,481 --> 00:38:53,080
thanks in large part to the little red bean called azuki.

558
00:38:58,900 --> 00:39:01,280
It doesn't matter how sweet they taste.

559
00:39:02,520 --> 00:39:04,580
Beans have one significant downside.

560
00:39:05,160 --> 00:39:06,020
It's the gas.

561
00:39:06,960 --> 00:39:08,900
And we don't mean biofuel.

562
00:39:11,420 --> 00:39:16,400
In the United States, it's a southern tradition to eat black-eyed peas on New Year's Day

563
00:39:16,401 --> 00:39:18,280
to bring luck for the rest of the year.

564
00:39:18,281 --> 00:39:23,840
In Japan, roasted soybeans are thrown around homes on the eve of their first day of spring

565
00:39:23,841 --> 00:39:25,840
to ward off evil spirits.

566
00:39:27,020 --> 00:39:29,400
Beans will return on Modern Marvels.

567
00:39:32,620 --> 00:39:36,920
While the consumption of beans on a regular basis can reduce the risk of diabetes,

568
00:39:37,860 --> 00:39:39,740
heart disease, cancer, and obesity,

569
00:39:40,400 --> 00:39:43,100
there is that downside.

570
00:39:44,040 --> 00:39:46,220
Oh yes, the flatulence problem.

571
00:39:46,221 --> 00:39:48,320
We hear questions about that often.

572
00:39:49,100 --> 00:39:51,480
So why do beans cause gas in the first place?

573
00:39:52,160 --> 00:39:56,380
The bean contains fiber and a lot of other complex materials,

574
00:39:56,540 --> 00:39:59,800
in particular raphanose, which is a complex carbohydrate

575
00:39:59,801 --> 00:40:03,500
that is made up of three very simple components of sugar.

576
00:40:04,580 --> 00:40:07,740
As beans break down and pass through your digestive system,

577
00:40:08,440 --> 00:40:11,140
the small intestine extracts many of the bean's nutrients.

578
00:40:11,141 --> 00:40:18,140
But some of the complex carbohydrates in beans are too large for the small intestine to absorb,

579
00:40:18,141 --> 00:40:20,140
so they pass on to the large intestine.

580
00:40:20,141 --> 00:40:27,140
There's a lot of healthy bacteria there which then act on those carbohydrates, breaking them down.

581
00:40:27,141 --> 00:40:32,140
It's in the process of breaking down these carbohydrates that gas is produced.

582
00:40:32,141 --> 00:40:40,140
And the gas can range everything from carbon dioxide, hydrogen, nitrogen, as well as sometimes methane.

583
00:40:41,140 --> 00:40:47,200
One method for reducing abdominal discomfort caused by beans is to soak them in water overnight.

584
00:40:48,720 --> 00:40:51,060
Many of the complex sugars release into the water.

585
00:40:52,540 --> 00:40:56,300
Then discard the soak water and rinse the beans before cooking in fresh water.

586
00:40:59,720 --> 00:41:03,880
Since 1990, science has provided a solution to the gas problem

587
00:41:03,881 --> 00:41:09,280
by adding a few drops of a product called Beano to beans and other gas-causing foods.

588
00:41:09,281 --> 00:41:16,200
The important thing to remember about Bino is that it's a gas preventer, not a gas reliever.

589
00:41:16,560 --> 00:41:20,320
And it's the only product on the market that prevents gas before it starts.

590
00:41:21,240 --> 00:41:26,840
Bino employs a mold called Aspergillus niger to provide the necessary enzyme the body lacks.

591
00:41:28,700 --> 00:41:31,620
Bino works by a process called enzymatic action.

592
00:41:32,280 --> 00:41:37,900
And effectively what this does is break apart these very large molecules into much simpler materials

593
00:41:37,901 --> 00:41:39,720
that can be readily absorbed by the body.

594
00:41:40,440 --> 00:41:43,940
We can thank the lactose intolerant for Beano's inspiration.

595
00:41:44,740 --> 00:41:48,640
A guy named Alan Kligerman conceived of the idea of Beano

596
00:41:48,641 --> 00:41:51,020
after first thinking of lactate.

597
00:41:51,240 --> 00:41:54,940
And lactate helps people enjoy dairy foods and digest them easily.

598
00:41:55,300 --> 00:41:58,600
When moving on to Beano, he realized that a different type of product

599
00:41:58,601 --> 00:42:01,700
would enable people to more easily digest beans

600
00:42:01,701 --> 00:42:04,020
and other kind of healthy, crunchy foods.

601
00:42:04,021 --> 00:42:10,040
In 1994, Beano began offering tablets to anti-flatulence fans.

602
00:42:10,560 --> 00:42:11,420
And aren't we all?

603
00:42:12,360 --> 00:42:15,220
Today, the latest version of Beano is the flip-top chewable.

604
00:42:16,060 --> 00:42:20,980
You can keep it in your pocket, keep it in your purse, and no one knows that you're taking Beano.

605
00:42:22,080 --> 00:42:25,140
While taking Beano to prevent gas may save you some embarrassment,

606
00:42:26,240 --> 00:42:29,020
history has no shortage of flatulence-friendly tales.

607
00:42:29,021 --> 00:42:34,340
The followers of Pythagoras would never eat beans

608
00:42:34,341 --> 00:42:36,600
But Greek physician Hippocrates claimed

609
00:42:36,601 --> 00:42:39,460
Passing gas is necessary to well-being

610
00:42:39,461 --> 00:42:43,180
The Roman emperor Claudius equally declared

611
00:42:43,181 --> 00:42:47,820
That all Roman citizens shall be allowed to pass gas whenever necessary

612
00:42:47,821 --> 00:42:51,380
However, during Emperor Constantine's reign

613
00:42:51,381 --> 00:42:53,560
The decision was reversed

614
00:42:53,561 --> 00:42:56,240
Making it illegal to pass gas in public

615
00:42:56,241 --> 00:43:03,320
One great story was that Benjamin Franklin, one of our founding fathers, wrote a letter

616
00:43:03,321 --> 00:43:08,360
to the Royal Academy of Brussels suggesting that we needed to deal with this problem and

617
00:43:08,361 --> 00:43:13,600
actually suggested adding a substance to foods that cause gas.

618
00:43:13,601 --> 00:43:18,120
In essence, Ben Franklin thought of Beano way back in the 1700s.

619
00:43:18,121 --> 00:43:25,920
So despite the legumes one airy drawback, no other crop can be baked or pureed, boiled

620
00:43:25,921 --> 00:43:30,100
or ground, drunk, fried, or refried.

621
00:43:30,101 --> 00:43:32,940
Become the main entree and the dessert.

622
00:43:32,941 --> 00:43:37,940
Provide power, protection, and protein, like the bean.

